---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy and security"
  description="What stays on your machine, what leaves for your model provider, and the safety boundaries still being built in Veasel Code."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="kicker">TRUST / DATA FLOW</p>
    <h1>
      Know what moves.
      <br />
      <em>Keep the reins.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel Code runs its server locally and stores session history in SQLite.
      Model prompts are sent to the provider configured by the person running
      the server. Local storage does not mean local inference.
    </p>
    <div class="data-flow" aria-label="Current message data flow">
      <div>
        <small>YOU</small>
        <strong>Terminal client</strong>
        <span>loopback HTTP</span>
      </div>
      <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
      <div>
        <small>LOCAL MACHINE</small>
        <strong>V server + SQLite</strong>
        <span>session history</span>
      </div>
      <b aria-hidden="true">→</b>
      <div>
        <small>YOUR CONFIGURED PROVIDER</small>
        <strong>Model API</strong>
        <span>prompt and recent context</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Current protections</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          The backend binds to loopback; remote server binding is not
          implemented.
        </li>
        <li>
          Provider credentials stay in the backend environment and are not
          returned by the API.
        </li>
        <li>
          Remote model endpoints require HTTPS; local development endpoints may
          use loopback HTTP.
        </li>
        <li>
          Provider redirects are rejected, and response sizes and message counts
          are bounded.
        </li>
        <li>
          New sessions accept an existing workspace directory and store its
          canonical path.
        </li>
        <li>
          Read-only workspace listing, file reads, and literal search stay
          inside that root, skip symlinks during traversal, and enforce file,
          byte, and result limits.
        </li>
        <li>
          Provider tool calls are limited to 6 rounds and 12 calls per session
          turn, with caps on arguments, accumulated results, and context size.
          No file-write or shell tool is exposed.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>What to keep in mind</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Your model provider receives the prompt and conversation history
          needed to answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          The loopback API has no application token; other programs running as
          your user may reach it and read files beneath an active session root.
        </li>
        <li>
          The model may request reads from the selected workspace. Returned
          excerpts and tool results are sent to your configured provider. These
          tools do not provide a filesystem sandbox against other processes
          running as your user.
        </li>
        <li>
          Plugin support remains partial: enabled Skill instructions can enter
          model context, but MCP processes and plugin trust controls are not
          available.
        </li>
        <li>
          The official mascot artwork carries a noncommercial license;
          commercial distribution needs separate permission.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <aside class="callout">
      <strong>Read-only by default as the product grows.</strong> Repository
      content and tool output are treated as untrusted data. File changes, shell
      execution, and plugin effects require explicit policy and approval before
      they are enabled.
    </aside>
    <p class="doc-next">
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/security/threat-model.md"
      >
        Read the threat model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/plugins/`}>
        Explore plugin safety <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
